30,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shion,,"As I suspected, the room is a failure. The wall is practically transparent to sound, and the mess has migrated to our desks.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found out we're paying a lot for outside rentals. 68,000 yen just because we can't use our own room for certain things.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I knew it! Two people are basically camping in there, and the rest of us are cleaning up the crumbs at our desks! It's totally unfair!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My friends, the data shows a deeper hunger. We have no place for the difficult truths, and our new colleagues remain strangers to us.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The outside hire costs are a symptom of inefficiency. More concerning is that the maintenance burden is unevenly distributed across the floor.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Servas, ""hunger"" is irrelevant. The fact is that we are hearing everything that happens in there. It's a privacy nightmare and a distraction.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"The fit-out quotes are... quite high. One is 141,000 and the other is 96,000. I'm worried about who has to sign for that.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,Why should we pay for a fancy fit-out if the people using it won't even pick up their trash? We need a rule about cleaning!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"A wall can block sound, but it can also block the spirit. If we only seek silence, we may find ourselves in a very lonely office.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the fit-out cost is a one-time expense. I am more concerned with the recurring loss of hours spent on upkeep and walking.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shion,,"If we want productivity, we must eliminate the noise. A dedicated, soundproofed space is the only logical path forward.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think I agree. If we spend the money now on a professional fit-out, we can stop paying those monthly outside hire fees.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I'll agree to a fit-out if it means we get a schedule! No more ""first come, first served."" Everyone should have a turn!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Let us consider a space that invites us to speak. A place where an awkward conversation can be resolved in private, rather than in public.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,We must ensure the chosen option doesn't create a new maintenance vacuum. I will not support a plan that relies on unpaid labor.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shion,,"We are circling the same point. The room needs a singular, defined purpose to stop the overlap and the noise.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I just want to make sure we have the figures on paper. If we can prove it saves money in the long run, it's easier to justify.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"Just make sure the ""purpose"" includes a cleaning chart! I'm not doing all the bins!","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Let us look at the options with a heart open to the needs of the people, not just the needs of the building.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I have seen enough. The current inefficiency is costing us more in time and money than a proper investment would.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
