60,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option B is the only logical choice. It solves the noise issue by regulating use and justifies the fit-out cost by replacing outside rentals.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Option B is best too. The 68,000 yen we spent outside is a lot. Having a professional meeting space makes sense.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option B has a calendar! That means no one can just hog the room. If we have a schedule, it's fair for everyone!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Servas,,"A meeting space is a start, but let us ensure it is not just for ""business."" It must be a sanctuary for the heart and the hard conversations.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option B is the most efficient. It centralizes the activity and eliminates the wasted hours spent traveling to outside hire locations.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Servas, as long as the door closes and the sound stays inside, you can call it a sanctuary. The priority is the office environment.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm still a bit nervous about the cost, but... seeing the outside hire invoices makes me realize we're already losing money.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"I just want to make sure that ""Meeting Space"" doesn't mean ""Place where people leave coffee cups."" We need a rule!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Servas,,"If we create a space for connection, the respect for that space will follow. Let us vote for a place where we can finally know one another.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,The maintenance for a meeting room is minimal compared to a kitchen. Option A would be a disaster for the floor's upkeep.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shion,,Option A is out of the question. More food in the room means more crumbs at our desks. It's a logical failure.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I agree. Option C is too passive. We actually need a place to work and talk, otherwise we'll keep paying for those outside rooms.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"Option C is boring! You can't have a schedule for ""sitting alone."" Option B is the only one that's fair and organized!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Servas,,"While silence has its value, our current silence is a wall between us. We must choose the path that allows us to break that wall.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,Option B minimizes the hidden labor of upkeep while maximizing the utility of the square footage. It is the only sustainable choice.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shion,,It seems we are in agreement. The evidence of noise pollution and financial waste points directly to a regulated meeting space.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I feel... better about this now. If we have a formal plan and a budget, I can support it.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,Yay! A calendar and a plan! I'll help make the cleaning chart for the meeting room!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Servas,,"May this room become a bridge between us, where we can speak the truths that have been left unsaid for too long.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,The decision is clear. Efficiency and cost-reduction align here. Let us vote.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
